  "notes": [
    "Provenance: seeded demonstration content authored for the Concept2Cure launch demo (fictional manufacturer, fictional device). Not model-drafted — no AI provider is configured.",
    "Seed identity: jonmichaelpsmith@gmail.com (user 1, organisation 2).",
    "FINDING: Projects: GET /api/c2c/projects/:id returns program_type, indication and intended_use but none of the device taxonomy intake stored (device_class, regulatory_path, product_code, predicate_devices, product_type, reviewPanel / regulationNumber / deviceFlags in metadata) — so no launch surface can show the class, product code, regulation or predicate the wizard captured.",
    "FINDING: Authoring/Review: reviews requested through POST /api/authoring/documents/:id/request-review do not appear on GET /api/review/board (the read model behind /concept2cure/review) — the two stores are separate (VSR-001 F-6).",
    "FINDING: Submission Center: the sequence/leaf model is the eCTD one. PUT /api/submissions/sequences/:id/leaves refuses a non-CTD-shaped sectionCode — \"estar.device-description\" answered HTTP 400 Section code \"estar.device-description\" does not name a CTD section a document can be filed at. Use a CTD section code — for example 1.2, 2.7.3 or 3.2.S.4.2 — since it decides where the document is filed in the package.  — and the builder presents eCTD modules. There is no eSTAR section vocabulary on the leaf route, so this pack files the device documents at the closest CTD codes (3.2.P.1, 3.2.R, 5.3.1.4, 5.3.5.2, 1.16, 1.14) with eSTAR documentType tokens; an authoring document cannot be placed as a leaf at all (authoring_documents is not a placeable table).",
    "FINDING: Submission Center: GET /sequences/:id/pathway-readiness?pathway=estar_510k reports every eSTAR section missing although six leaves carry eSTAR documentType tokens — the route maps leaves without the `substantive` flag the mapper requires (server/routes/submissions.ts pathway-readiness → estar-mapper EstarInputLeaf.substantive: undefined ⇒ not substantive, fail-closed), so a vault-backed leaf can never mark a section present here.",
    "FINDING: Submission Readiness: the structural validation flags every vault-backed leaf UNRESOLVED_DOCUMENT (\"has no resolvable document\") — 6 of 6. The leaf route accepted documentTable vault_documents + documentUuid and pinned documentContentSha256, and vault_documents is in RESOLVABLE_DOCUMENT_TABLES, but documentPointerFindings (server/services/ectd/dispatch-readiness.ts) tests the integer documentId only, which is null for a uuid-keyed vault document. Consequence: a sequence built from uploaded vault documents can never clear the dispatch gate on this build.",
    "FINDING: QMS: GET /api/mdx/qms/changes returns rows without their cross-references (no \"links\" field) while GET /api/mdx/qms/changes/:id carries 3; the Change control log (client/src/concept2cure/quality/ChangeControl.tsx linkCount = c.links?.length ?? 0) therefore shows 0 links for MDX-CC-2026-001 until the row is expanded.",
    "FINDING: QMS: the launch QMS API has no CAPA create route — CAPA records are read-only through GET /api/mdx/postmarket (capa_records) and can only be referenced from a change-control link (linkType \"capa\"). No CAPA record was seeded.",
    "FINDING: Audit trail: the server chain verdict for this tenant is ok=false ({\"id\":\"6633e4a6-0fbc-400f-b9e1-600acd237b02\",\"expected\":\"17695c41673a4cfdbfa7f4a449827b64f7c08d706519f6adc2cb326e62a91302\",\"stored\":\"888f94de61c74f00a7a0540d1f54d851fbadb762f18592d855033a06030259f8\",\"tenantId\":2,\"segment\":\"legacy\",\"commitsTo\":null}) — a pre-existing state of this database's audit_logs, not caused by this pack; every entry this pack wrote carries hash and prevHash (0 unchained).",
    "FINDING: Projects: intake creates a canonical submission spine for drug application types only (server/routes/c2c/project-intake.ts DRUG_APPLICATION_TYPES); a 510(k) program gets none, so this pack creates the Submission Center entry itself, keyed by the program name.",
    "FINDING: Authoring: POST /api/authoring/docs with client_program_id binds the new document to the program's ONE governed c2c_document, so a second document for the same program is refused 409 DOCUMENT_ALIAS_CONFLICT (\"c2c_documents doc_… is already recorded as a different document. Nothing was created.\"). The SE Discussion and the Cybersecurity Summary were created without client_program_id (org-wide, unbound); the Authoring surface lists them only when no program is open.",
    "Purge coverage: QMS documents are retired and the change-control record deleted through the API; the program, vault documents, authoring documents, submission and sequence have no delete/archive endpoint in the launch API (see purge.retained)."
  ],
  "finishedAt": "2026-09-21T18:04:04.728Z"
